From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yash Dayani <52958495+YashDayani@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:18:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: theme list dialogs with Material You colors

Theme.AlertDialog (used by every list popup in Settings sub-pages,
including Evolver) inherits AppCompat's dialog without an accent or
background, so the popups showed AppCompat's teal radio buttons on a flat
grey surface. Use the same accent and surface as
Theme.AlertDialog.SettingsLib.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 res/values/themes.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/res/values/themes.xml b/res/values/themes.xml
index e512f75..bbf839d 100644
--- a/res/values/themes.xml
+++ b/res/values/themes.xml
@@ -129,6 +129,11 @@
         <item name="android:windowTitleStyle">@*android:style/DialogWindowTitle.DeviceDefault</item>
         <item name="android:textAppearanceMedium">@style/TextAppearance.DialogMessage</item>
         <item name="buttonBarButtonStyle">@*android:style/Widget.DeviceDefault.Button.ButtonBar.AlertDialog</item>
+
+        <!-- Material You accent and surface, as in Theme.AlertDialog.SettingsLib. Without them
+             AppCompat falls back to teal radio buttons on a flat grey dialog. -->
+        <item name="colorAccent">@color/settingslib_dialog_accent</item>
+        <item name="android:colorBackground">@color/settingslib_dialog_background</item>
     </style>
 
 
